# Content

## Post formats

Posts live in `src/content/posts/` with frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "Define 'Boom' Please"
date: 2026-05-25T20:00:00Z
# use ISO datetime so newer posts reliably sort to the top
# format: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
type: essay        # essay | linked | notes | review
tags: [apple, ai]
star: true         # originals only; linked posts: false
linkUrl: "https://…"
linkAuthor: "Tripp Mickle"
---
```

### Type rules

- **essay** — original. `star: true`. DF-style long or medium form; short
  paragraphs, clear thesis. See `writing-style.mdc`.
- **linked** — external piece + your take. Requires `linkUrl`. **Title
  links to `linkUrl`** (not the on-site permalink). Body: attribution →
  brief setup → **one** blockquote → commentary. Never summarize the whole
  source.
- **notes** — 1–3 paragraphs, one idea. No required blockquote.
- **review** — verdict first, evidence second. Use sparingly.

## Ordering

- Newest posts must appear first on `/`, `/archive`, and `/feed.xml`.
- When two posts are on the same day, set different `date` times so order is explicit.

## Voice (editorial)

Follow `writing-style.mdc` (Daring Fireball–style). In short:

- Punchy, opinionated, no hedging
- Link posts add value; they don't echo the source
- No marketing language, emoji, or welcome intros

## UI copy

- Nav: `/latest`, `/archive`, `/feed.xml` (no `/notes` or `/sponsor` in v1)
- Page eyebrows match URL path
- Section headings: uppercase mono, 2–3 words
- CTAs: sentence case + arrow (`Reserve a week →`)
- Footer left: `© <year>` + linked X handle (`@bmbyslm` → `https://x.com/bmbyslm`)
- Footer right: `riphone · <route>` (or version on home)
- Site URL: `https://riphone.org`

## Don'ts

- No emoji in posts or UI
- No exclamation points in your voice (quoted speech OK)
- No "I think / I believe / in my opinion"
- No bare URLs or "click here" anchors
